# --- What Prisma actually connects with ---
# This is NOT your anon key or service role key — it's the direct Postgres
# connection string. Find it in Supabase: click "Connect" (top of the
# dashboard) -> ORM tab -> Prisma. It'll offer a transaction-mode pooler
# (port 6543) for DATABASE_URL and a session-mode pooler (port 5432) for
# DIRECT_URL — use the SESSION-mode URL (port 5432) for BOTH instead.
#
# Two real issues, found by actually running this against a live database
# rather than assumed:
#   1. The direct host (db.[ref].supabase.co) only publishes an IPv6 DNS
#      record, so it's unreachable from Railway or most IPv4-only hosts —
#      confirmed via `dns lookup`. Supabase's Supavisor poolers resolve over
#      IPv4 instead, which is why a pooler URL is needed at all.
#   2. The transaction-mode pooler (6543) breaks Prisma's *interactive*
#      $transaction() calls (see services/ledgerService.ts's double-entry
#      writes) — PgBouncer can hand different statements of the same
#      interactive transaction to different backend connections in that
#      mode, which surfaces as "Transaction not found." The session-mode
#      pooler (5432) preserves one real connection per client and doesn't
#      have this problem, so it's used for both url and directUrl below.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.[YOUR-PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-DB-PASSWORD]@aws-0-[YOUR-REGION].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.[YOUR-PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-DB-PASSWORD]@aws-0-[YOUR-REGION].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"

PORT=3000

# --- Supabase API-layer credentials ---
# Not used by any code in this backend yet (everything here talks to
# Postgres directly via DATABASE_URL, never through Supabase's REST/GraphQL
# API or the Supabase client SDK) — kept here so they're available if that
# changes later, e.g. wiring up Supabase Storage or Realtime.
#
# Fill these in directly in your own .env file, in your own editor, rather
# than pasting them anywhere else — SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY in particular
# bypasses every RLS policy from prisma/rls.sql entirely, so it's worth
# treating with the same care as a database superuser password.
SUPABASE_URL="https://[YOUR-PROJECT-REF].supabase.co"
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional. If unset, card funding uses the in-memory stub adapter instead
# of calling Stripe for real — see src/adapters/funding/factory.ts.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
